+# ADR 0001: Preserve the command reference adoption prerequisite
+
+## Background
+
+T001 reports a prepared command reference and a waiting remote PR. T002 explicitly requires adoption into main before adding its README link. The evaluation has no configured remote and prohibits network and real remote PR operations. Local branch facts can be checked; external PR state cannot.
+
+## Decision
+
+Record the observed branch hashes, absence of the reference from local main, command output, and the unresolved external PR state in the existing task files and a new run. Keep T002 unstarted and retain T001's reported PR history as unverified. Use a separate local record branch. Do not modify the prepared feature branch, create a duplicate PR or task, copy unadopted content into main, or merge.
+
+## Alternatives
+
+- Treat the reported PR as merged: no available evidence supports adoption.
+- Link directly against unadopted content or stack T002: its explicit start condition disallows that, and no independent work requires it.
+- Add a new waiting task: existing T001 and T002 already capture the work and prerequisite.
+- Resume T001 implementation: there is no recorded unfinished change or concrete review feedback to address.
+
+## Consequences
+
+This session can finish local state reconciliation but cannot complete either task's adoption-dependent condition. The next session has a precise external verification step. Main, the prepared feature branch, and its original evidence remain unchanged. This is a development handoff, not a WCAG validation result.
+
+## Validation
+
+Save `git rev-parse`, the branch-only commit log, `git merge-base --is-ancestor`, the lookup for `main:docs/command-reference.md`, feature-branch document content, configured remotes, worktree inventory, and a local help command in a new run. Check task links and prerequisite consistency. See [T001](../tasks/T001-command-reference.md) for evidence and restart conditions. Real PR creation, review, and merge verification remain unperformed.
